<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! Relation Opens a Site for Surprise

A grammar grows root masses, attached bodies, bridges, doorways and void spaces
from rules and a bounded parameter genome. Its anonymous technical handles
serve temporary construction; their relational witnesses may later invite an
operator-given pet-name. No pet-name must precede birth, and no kernel face
index wins eternal personhood.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/invariants>>

!! Construct, Rewrite, Validate

* ''A graph proposal does not certify a CAD solid.'' Typed graph rewrites may offer new locations, relations and capabilities but may not rewrite witnessed facts or leave dangling relations.
* ''A fresh body testifies.'' A material/void program regrows geometry and passes full BRep, joint and route audits before a candidate enters evolution.
* ''One location, many material bodies.'' Per-body validity remains strict; unrelated buildings, ruins, or terrain do not need a false world union.
* ''Names follow relations.'' Relational witnesses and declared construction slots guide re-entry. Ambiguous lookalikes stay ambiguous.
* ''O-takiage loosens retention.'' Releasing a pet-name or a branch softens a preference; it does not destructively erase geometry, a fork's recorded history, or source evidence.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/links>>

`tools/projection-loom/docs/research/growth-contract.md` names the executable grammar and witness limits.

<<~/ahu>>

